{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"f4258b13f7798ffa","name":"card_event_radar_alert","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/Base/events/card_event_radar_alert","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"RADAR ALERT","text":"When the enemy deploys a unit, add a random British air unit of similar cost.","flavorText":"The British radar air defense system was code-named Chain Home and served as the backbone in their defense during the Battle of Britain. The system consisted of a ring of coastal radar installations, each with a maximum range of 322 km (200 miles), which meant they could detect German formations all the way to their bases in occupied France. This provided the RAF with nearly a half hour of lead time which could be used to gather squadrons of fighters to intercept threats. Each radar installation sent out a stream of short-pulse radio waves which scattered upon striking an object, such as an aircraft, and some of the energy returned as an echo that was displayed on a cathode-ray tube. The time between transmission and echo reception was used to calculate the distance to the reflecting object.","faction":"Britain","type":"gotcha","rarity":"Rare","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_radar_alert","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_radar_alert_title","SourceString":"RADAR ALERT","LocalizedString":"RADAR ALERT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::gotcha","faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_radar_alert_text","SourceString":"When the enemy deploys a unit, add a random British air unit of similar cost.","LocalizedString":"When the enemy deploys a unit, add a random British air unit of similar cost."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_radar_alert_history","SourceString":"The British radar air defense system was code-named Chain Home and served as the backbone in their defense during the Battle of Britain. The system consisted of a ring of coastal radar installations, each with a maximum range of 322 km (200 miles), which meant they could detect German formations all the way to their bases in occupied France. This provided the RAF with nearly a half hour of lead time which could be used to gather squadrons of fighters to intercept threats. Each radar installation sent out a stream of short-pulse radio waves which scattered upon striking an object, such as an aircraft, and some of the energy returned as an echo that was displayed on a cathode-ray tube. The time between transmission and echo reception was used to calculate the distance to the reflecting object.","LocalizedString":"The British radar air defense system was code-named Chain Home and served as the backbone in their defense during the Battle of Britain. The system consisted of a ring of coastal radar installations, each with a maximum range of 322 km (200 miles), which meant they could detect German formations all the way to their bases in occupied France. This provided the RAF with nearly a half hour of lead time which could be used to gather squadrons of fighters to intercept threats. Each radar installation sent out a stream of short-pulse radio waves which scattered upon striking an object, such as an aircraft, and some of the energy returned as an echo that was displayed on a cathode-ray tube. The time between transmission and echo reception was used to calculate the distance to the reflecting object."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Basic","returnSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFromHand"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Class_Specific/War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2.0"},"soundAttack":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/